Ωª:ß*<≈!ã<- Y;ì*Ÿ<{"title": "ACEITE FRITO:El aceite que se ha empleado para fre\u00edr un producto que contenga gluten es un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten."}{"title": "PATATAS FRITAS:"}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N DE CELIACOS:An organization that provides information and support for individuals with celiac disease regarding gluten-free diets."}{"title": "COLEGIO:A school where considerations for gluten-free diets must be taken into account for celiac patients."}{"title": "PACIENTE CELIACO:An individual diagnosed with celiac disease who must adhere to a gluten-free diet."}{"title": "ACEITE:Aceite refers to oils, which are sources of dietary fats that can be categorized as either TCM (Traditional Chinese Medicine) or TCL (Traditional Chinese Lifestyle). It is an important ingredient in low-sodium diets, where it is utilized for cooking and dressing foods. In modified diets, specifically TCM oil is permitted, highlighting its significance in dietary practices. However, when selecting oils for cooking, it is essential to choose them carefully to avoid gluten contamination, ensuring that they align with dietary restrictions and health considerations."}{"title": "FESTIVIDAD:An occasion where food is served, which may pose a risk for celiac patients if gluten-containing items are present."}{"title": "GLOSINAS:Sweets that may contain gluten and should be avoided by celiac patients."}{"title": "NUTRISON EST\u00c1NDAR:Nutrison Est\u00e1ndar is a brand of nutritional supplements that cater to patients requiring dietary adjustments, particularly for gluten and lactose intolerance."}{"title": "FRESUBIN:Fresubin is a brand under Fresenius Kabi that specializes in producing a diverse range of nutritional drinks and products. These offerings are specifically designed to cater to patients with dietary restrictions, including individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "EDANEC:Edanec is a nutritional supplement brand that provides products suitable for individuals with gluten and lactose intolerance."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE CHRON:Chron's disease is an inflammatory bowel disease that can present symptoms similar to celiac disease and may require differential diagnosis."}{"title": "YEYUNITIS ULCERATIVA:Ulcerative jejunitis is a condition that can be associated with severe malabsorption and may occur in patients with refractory celiac disease."}{"title": "LINFOMA:Lymphoma is a type of cancer that primarily affects the lymphatic system, which is a crucial part of the immune system. This condition can lead to various complications, including ascitis quilosa, a specific type of fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity. Additionally, lymphoma may be associated with refractory celiac disease, and it can present with gastrointestinal symptoms, highlighting its potential impact on digestive health."}{"title": "ATROFIA VELLOSITARIA:Villus atrophy is a condition characterized by the flattening of the intestinal villi, commonly seen in patients with celiac disease."}{"title": "GASTROENTERITIS EOSINOF\u00cdLICA:Gastroenteritis eosinof\u00edlica is an inflammatory condition of the gastrointestinal tract that is associated with food allergies. It can occur at any age and is characterized by severe gastrointestinal symptoms. A key feature of this condition is the presence of eosinophils in gastric or intestinal biopsies, which helps in its diagnosis."}{"title": "AGA INSTITUTE:The AGA Institute is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the science and practice of gastroenterology."}{"title": "COELIAC DISEASE:Celiac disease is a chronic autoimmune disorder that occurs in genetically predisposed people where the ingestion of gluten leads to damage in the small intestine."}{"title": "GODDARD:C.J. Goddard is a researcher who has studied the complications associated with celiac disease."}{"title": "HEIKKIL\u00c4:K. Heikkil\u00e4 is a researcher who has conducted studies on the relationship between celiac disease and bone fractures."}{"title": "NIH CONSENSUS CONFERENCE:The NIH Consensus Development Conference on Celiac Disease is a meeting that aims to provide a comprehensive review of the current knowledge and management of celiac disease."}{"title": "ASKLING:J. Askling is a researcher who has studied cancer incidence in individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "NIEWINSKI:M. Niewinski is an expert in celiac disease and gluten-free diets, contributing to advancements in the field."}{"title": "SCOTT:E.M. Scott is a researcher with a focus on developing guidelines for osteoporosis in patients with celiac disease. In addition to this work, Scott has also conducted a trial examining the costs and consequences associated with systematic nutrition team follow-up after percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy. Through these efforts, Scott contributes to advancing knowledge and improving patient care in both osteoporosis management and nutritional support in clinical settings."}{"title": "FASANO:"}{"title": "ANA M\u00aa M\u00c1RQUEZ ARMENTEROS:Ana M\u00aa M\u00e1rquez Armenteros is a specialist in pediatric gastroenterology at Hospital Materno Infantil, focusing on the diagnosis and follow-up of metabolic disorders."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO INFANTA CRISTINA:Hospital Universitario Infanta Cristina is a healthcare institution in Badajoz, specializing in clinical nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "HOSPITAL MATERNO INFANTIL:Hospital Materno Infantil is a medical facility in Badajoz that specializes in pediatric care and the diagnosis of metabolic disorders."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE EXTREMADURA:Universidad de Extremadura is an educational institution in Badajoz, focusing on biomedical sciences and medical education."}{"title": "HOMOCISTINURIA:Homocystinuria is a metabolic disorder resulting from a deficiency in cystathionine beta-synthase, leading to the accumulation of homocysteine."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ORINA DE JARABE DE ARCE:The \"ENFERMEDAD DE ORINA DE JARABE DE ARCE,\" known as Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD), is an amino acid metabolism disorder. It is characterized by a deficiency in the branched-chain alpha-keto acid dehydrogenase complex. This deficiency results in the accumulation of specific amino acids in the body, which can lead to various health complications."}{"title": "ERRORRES INNATOS DEL CICLO DE LA UREA:Urea cycle disorders are genetic conditions that result in a deficiency of one of the enzymes in the urea cycle, leading to the accumulation of ammonia in the body."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOSIS:GLUCOGENOSIS refers to a group of diseases known as glycogen storage diseases, which are characterized by alterations in glycogen synthesis or degradation. These metabolic disorders arise from defects in the enzymes responsible for glycogen synthesis and breakdown, resulting in the excessive accumulation of glycogen in various tissues. The underlying cause of glucogenosis is typically enzyme deficiencies that disrupt normal glycogen metabolism, leading to abnormal storage of glycogen in the body."}{"title": "METABOLOPAT\u00cdAS:Metabolic disorders are conditions that disrupt normal metabolism, leading to the accumulation of toxic substances in the body due to enzyme deficiencies."}{"title": "BADAJOZ:"}{"title": "PAH:Phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH) is an essential enzyme that plays a critical role in the metabolism of phenylalanine, converting it into tyrosine. A deficiency in PAH is the underlying cause of phenylketonuria (PKU), a genetic disorder that can lead to serious health issues if not managed properly. In the context of treatment, the functional gene for PAH is introduced in gene therapy to address this deficiency in patients with PKU."}{"title": "BH4:Tetrahydrobiopterin is a cofactor necessary for the activity of phenylalanine hydroxylase and is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine."}{"title": "DHPR:Dihydropteridine reductase is an enzyme that plays a role in the regeneration of tetrahydrobiopterin, which is crucial for neurotransmitter synthesis."}{"title": "PKU:Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a genetic and metabolic disorder characterized by the accumulation of phenylalanine in the body. If left untreated, this accumulation can lead to severe neurological issues. To prevent such damage, individuals with PKU require careful dietary management to control their phenylalanine levels."}{"title": "HPA:Hyperphenylalaninemia benign (HPA) is a mild form of phenylketonuria characterized by lower levels of phenylalanine that do not require dietary treatment."}{"title": "IVS10:IVS10 is the most common mutation associated with phenylketonuria in Southern Europe, affecting the PAH gene."}{"title": "CROMOSOMA 12:Chromosome 12 is where the PAH gene is located, which is responsible for phenylketonuria."}{"title": "DIAGNOSTICO BIOQUIMICO:Biochemical diagnosis of phenylketonuria is established through the measurement of plasma phenylalanine levels."}{"title": "CASEN RECORDATI:Casen Recordati is a commercial entity that produces special formulas for low-Phe diets in Spain."}{"title": "MEAD-JHONSON:Mead-Jhonson is a company that offers various products for managing phenylketonuria (PKU) diets."}{"title": "MILUPA SA:Milupa SA is a manufacturer of specialized dietary products for patients with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "NUTRICIA SA:Nutricia SA provides nutritional products tailored for individuals with dietary restrictions, including those with PKU."}{"title": "SCIENTIFIC HOSPITAL SUPPLIES (SHS):Scientific Hospital Supplies (SHS) offers a range of dietary products for managing phenylketonuria."}{"title": "VITAFLO ESPA\u00d1A:Vitaflo Espa\u00f1a specializes in nutritional products for patients with metabolic disorders, including PKU."}{"title": "PHENYLKETONURIA (PKU):Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a metabolic disorder that requires dietary management to avoid phenylalanine."}{"title": "FENILALANINA:Fenilalanina is an amino acid that must be managed in the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "TIROSINA:Tirosina is an amino acid that can be supplemented in the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "BIOTERINA:Biopterina is a cofactor involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine."}{"title": "NEOPTERINA:Neopterina is a compound related to the metabolism of phenylalanine."}{"title": "GTP:GTP is a molecule involved in various metabolic processes, including those related to phenylalanine."}{"title": "PKU ANAMIX JUNIOR:PKU Anamix Junior is a dietary product for children aged 1-10 years with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "PKU ANAMIX JUNIOR LQ:PKU Anamix Junior LQ is a liquid formula for children aged 3-10 years with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "CASEN FLEET PKU1:Casen Fleet PKU1 is a powdered dietary product for managing phenylketonuria."}{"title": "CASEN FLEET PKU GEL:Casen Fleet PKU Gel is a gel-based dietary product for individuals with phenylketonuria, suitable for those over 6 months."}{"title": "MEAD-JOHNSON PHENYL-FREE 1:Mead-Johnson Phenyl-Free 1 is a dietary product designed for infants with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "MEAD-JOHNSON PHENYL-FREE 2:Mead-Johnson Phenyl-Free 2 is a dietary product for older children and adults with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "FLEETPKU-AVANT:FleetPKU-Avant is a specialized formula for managing phenylketonuria."}{"title": "FLEETPKU-PLUS:FleetPKU-Plus is a dietary product designed for individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "VITAFLO PKU COOLER 10:Vitaflo PKU Cooler 10 is a liquid dietary product for individuals over 3 years old with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "VITAFLO PKU COOLER 15:Vitaflo PKU Cooler 15 is a liquid dietary product for individuals over 3 years old with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "VITAFLO PKU COOLER 20:Vitaflo PKU Cooler 20 is a liquid dietary product for individuals over 3 years old with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "SHS PHLEXY-10:SHS Phlexy-10 is a dietary product available in various forms for individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "SHS PHLEXY-10 BARS:SHS Phlexy-10 bars are a snack option for individuals managing phenylketonuria."}{"title": "SHS PHLEXY-10 TABLETS:SHS Phlexy-10 tablets are a dietary supplement for individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "SHS PHLEXY-10 CAPSULES:SHS Phlexy-10 capsules are a dietary supplement for individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "FLEETPKU-AVANT MONODOSIS:FleetPKU-Avant Monodosis is a single-dose dietary product for managing phenylketonuria."}{"title": "MEAD-JOHNSON PHENYL-FREE 2 HP:Mead-Johnson Phenyl-Free 2 HP is a high-protein dietary product for individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "PKU LOPHLEX LQ 10:PKU Lophlex LQ 10 is a liquid dietary product for individuals over 4 years old with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "PKU LOPHLEX LQ 20:PKU Lophlex LQ 20 is a liquid dietary product for individuals over 4 years old with phenylketonuria, including pregnant women.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "L-TIROSINA:L-Tirosina is a non-essential amino acid that is produced from phenylalanine and plays a crucial role in the production of neurotransmitters. It is often included in nutritional discussions due to its importance in various physiological processes. Additionally, L-Tirosina may require supplementation in certain cases, particularly for individuals with phenylketonuria, a genetic disorder that affects the metabolism of phenylalanine."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RESTRINGIDOS:Alimentos restringidos are foods that are high in phenylalanine and should be limited in the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS LIBRES:Alimentos libres are foods that are low in phenylalanine and can be consumed freely by individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "QUESOS:Quesos refers to cheeses, which contain varying levels of phenylalanine and may need to be limited in the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria."}{"title": "PHE:Phe is an amino acid that can increase during periods of acute illness or surgical intervention, necessitating dietary adjustments."}{"title": "PNAVB:PNAVB refers to a type of protein that should be reduced in intake during certain medical conditions to manage Phe levels."}{"title": "CABALLA:Caballa refers to mackerel, a type of fish that is commonly consumed."}{"title": "CONEJO:Conejo is Spanish for rabbit, which is a type of meat that can be included in various diets."}{"title": "CACAHUETES TOSTADOS:Cacahuetes tostados are roasted peanuts, often eaten as a snack."}{"title": "QUESO PARMESANO:Queso parmesano is a hard cheese originating from Italy, used in various culinary applications."}{"title": "COLIFLOR COCIDA:Coliflor cocida refers to cooked cauliflower, a vegetable often included in diets."}{"title": "D\u00d3NUT:D\u00f3nut is a type of fried dough confection, typically sweet and often consumed as a dessert or snack."}{"title": "CALAMAR:Calamar refers to squid, which is a seafood item commonly eaten."}{"title": "CORAZ\u00d3N DE BUEY:Coraz\u00f3n de buey is a type of beef heart, which can be used in various dishes."}{"title": "COSTILLAS DE CORDERO:Costillas de cordero are lamb ribs, a popular meat choice in many cuisines."}{"title": "QUESO GRUYERE:Queso gruyere is a Swiss cheese known for its distinct flavor, often used in cooking."}{"title": "CORN-FLAKES MUY AZUCARADOS:Corn-flakes muy azucarados are sugary corn-flakes, a sweetened breakfast option."}{"title": "FRANCFORT:Francfort refers to a type of sausage, commonly known as a hot dog."}{"title": "FOIE-GRAS:Foie-gras is a luxury food product made from the liver of a duck or goose, often considered a delicacy."}{"title": "H\u00cdGADO DE CERDO CRUDO:H\u00edgado de cerdo crudo refers to raw pork liver, which can be used in various dishes."}{"title": "CHORIZO:Chorizo is a type of spicy sausage originating from Spain, used in many recipes."}{"title": "REDONDO DE TERNEA:Redondo de ternera refers to a cut of beef, often used in roasts."}{"title": "ESP\u00c1RRAGOS EN LATA:Esp\u00e1rragos en lata are canned asparagus, a convenient vegetable option."}{"title": "GALLETAS SALADAS:Galletas saladas are salty crackers, often consumed as a snack."}{"title": "GAMBAS CRUDAS:Gambas crudas refers to raw shrimp, a seafood item used in various dishes."}{"title": "CHULETA DE TERNEA:Chuleta de ternera refers to a veal chop, a cut of meat often grilled or roasted."}{"title": "ESPINACAS COCIDAS:Espinacas cocidas are cooked spinach, a nutritious vegetable."}{"title": "LECHE DE VACA EVAPORADA:Leche de vaca evaporada is evaporated milk, often used in cooking and baking."}{"title": "GARBANZOS COCIDOS:Garbanzos cocidos are cooked chickpeas, a common ingredient in many dishes."}{"title": "LENGUA DE CERDO:Lengua de cerdo refers to pork tongue, which can be prepared in various ways."}{"title": "CHULETA DE CERDO:Chuleta de cerdo is a pork chop, a popular meat choice."}{"title": "GALLETAS TIPO MAR\u00cdA:Galletas tipo mar\u00eda are a type of sweet biscuit, often used in desserts."}{"title": "LECHE CONDENSADA DE VACA:Leche condensada de vaca is sweetened condensed milk, used in desserts and beverages."}{"title": "HUEVO ENTERO:Huevo entero refers to a whole egg, which is a common ingredient in cooking. However, in the context of a modified diet, whole eggs are not permitted. It is important to note that whole eggs have a phosphorus ratio at the limit of 16 mg/g, and therefore, they are recommended to be consumed in moderation."}{"title": "FILETE DE TERNEA:Filete de ternera is a cut of veal, often grilled or pan-fried."}{"title": "HELADO DE VAINILLA:Helado de vainilla is vanilla ice cream, a popular dessert."}{"title": "LENTEJAS SECAS COCIDAS:Lentejas secas cocidas are cooked lentils, a nutritious legume."}{"title": "HUEVO FRITO:Huevo frito refers to a fried egg, a common breakfast item."}{"title": "PATO:PATO, which refers to duck, is a type of poultry commonly used in various cuisines. However, it is important to note that duck is not allowed in modified diets due to its potential health implications. Specifically, PATO, or duck, is a bird that can have a significant purine content, which may influence uric acid levels in individuals. Therefore, while PATO is a popular culinary choice, its consumption may be restricted for those managing dietary concerns related to purine intake."}{"title": "FILETE DE BUEY:Filete de buey is a cut of beef, often grilled or roasted."}{"title": "LECHE DE VACA:LECHE DE VACA refers to cow's milk, which is a staple in many diets and commonly used in the production of infant formulas. However, it is important to note that cow's milk may not be suitable for all infants and is generally recommended to be introduced only after the first year of age. The composition of cow's milk is regulated by specific norms to ensure its safety and nutritional adequacy for various uses, including infant feeding."}{"title": "MAGDALENAS:Magdalenas are Spanish muffins or cupcakes, often enjoyed as a snack."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdAS SECAS COCIDAS:Jud\u00edas secas cocidas are cooked dried beans, a common ingredient in many dishes."}{"title": "REQUET\u00d3N:Requet\u00f3n is a type of cheese, often used in cooking."}{"title": "HAMBURGUESAS:Hamburguesas are hamburgers, a popular fast food item."}{"title": "MORTADELA CON ACEITUNAS:Mortadela con aceitunas is a type of sausage with olives, often used in sandwiches."}{"title": "RI\u00d1\u00d3N DE TERNEA:Ri\u00f1\u00f3n de ternera is veal kidney, used in various culinary applications."}{"title": "LENGUADO CRUDO:Lenguado crudo refers to raw sole fish, which can be used in sushi or sashimi."}{"title": "SALCHICH\u00d3N:Salchich\u00f3n is a type of cured sausage, often sliced for sandwiches."}{"title": "H\u00cdGADO DE CORDERO:H\u00edgado de cordero refers to lamb liver, which can be prepared in various ways."}{"title": "LECHE DE OVEJA:Leche de oveja is sheep's milk, used in various cheeses and dishes."}{"title": "LUBINA:Lubina refers to sea"}{"title": "NAVB:NAVB is an organization involved in dietary management and treatment protocols for conditions like phenylketonuria (PKU)."}{"title": "PHENYLKETONURIA:Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a metabolic disorder that necessitates strict dietary management to prevent complications both during pregnancy and throughout an individual's life."}{"title": "GLUCOMACROPEPTIDE:Glucomacrop\u00e9ptido (GMP) is a dairy-derived peptide that contains very low amounts of phenylalanine and is used to improve dietary options for PKU patients."}{"title": "LNAA:LNAA is a therapeutic option designed to decrease the passage of phenylalanine (Phe) to the brain, making it particularly effective for patients with poor adherence to dietary restrictions. It refers to neutral amino acids that compete with phenylalanine for transport across the blood-brain barrier, thereby aiding in the management of phenylketonuria (PKU)."}{"title": "TYROSINE:Tyrosine is an amino acid that may be supplemented during pregnancy for women with PKU to support metabolic needs."}{"title": "CARNITINE:Carnitine is a nutrient that plays a significant role in metabolic processes and may be evaluated for potential deficiency in patients with Phenylketonuria. Additionally, it is administered during hyperammonemic crises to improve metabolic status in patients with glycogen storage diseases, also known as glucogenosis. This highlights the importance of carnitine in managing specific metabolic disorders and its potential therapeutic applications in clinical settings."}{"title": "L-PUFA:L-PUFA refers to long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids that may be considered for supplementation in the management of PKU."}{"title": "FETAL LIVER:The fetal liver is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine during pregnancy, particularly in the context of maternal PKU management."}{"title": "PHENYLALANINE:"}{"title": "ACIDO ALPHA-ISOCAPROICO:Alpha-isocaproic acid is a product of leucine metabolism and is involved in the MSUD metabolic pathway."}{"title": "ACIDO ALPHA-KETO-BETA-METILVALERICO:Alpha-keto-beta-methylvaleric acid is a product of isoleucine metabolism and is part of the MSUD metabolic pathway."}{"title": "ACIDO ALPHA-KETOISOVALERICO:Alpha-ketoisovaleric acid is a product of valine metabolism and is involved in the MSUD metabolic pathway."}{"title": "ISOVALERIL-COA:Isovaleryl-CoA is a compound in the metabolic pathway of branched-chain amino acids and is associated with isovaleric acidemia."}{"title": "PROPIONIL-COA:Propionyl-CoA is a compound in the metabolic pathway that is involved in propionic acidemia."}{"title": "SUCCINIL-COA:Succinyl-CoA is a compound in the metabolic pathway that is involved in methylmalonic acidemia."}{"title": "HIDROXILACI\u00d3N DE PHE:The hydroxylation of phenylalanine (Phe) is a metabolic process that is crucial for the proper metabolism of this amino acid."}{"title": "AMINO\u00c1CIDOS DE CADENA RAMIFICADA:Amino\u00e1cidos de cadena ramificada, commonly known as branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs), are essential amino acids that include leucine, isoleucine, and valine. These amino acids play a significant role in various metabolic processes and are particularly noted for their ability to enhance muscle mass and function, especially in elderly individuals. BCAAs are crucial for maintaining muscle health and may help in addressing metabolic disorders."}{"title": "CRISIS DE ATAXIA:Ataxia crisis is a clinical manifestation that can occur in adults with Maple Syrup Urine Disease during intercurrent processes."}{"title": "DETERMINACI\u00d3N DE AA EN SANGRE:Blood amino acid determination is a diagnostic procedure used to identify the presence of specific amino acids, such as aloisoleucine, in patients suspected of having metabolic disorders."}{"title": "BIOPSIA DE PIEL:Skin biopsy is a diagnostic procedure used to confirm enzyme deficiency in patients with metabolic disorders like PKU and MSUD."}{"title": "ESTUDIO MUTACIONAL:Mutational analysis is a genetic test performed to identify specific mutations associated with metabolic disorders such as PKU and MSUD."}{"title": "TERAPIA G\u00c9NICA:"}{"title": "BCAA:BCAA, or Branched-Chain Amino Acids, are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in muscle metabolism. They are significant in dietary management for metabolic disorders and are obtained from proteins found in food. These amino acids are vital for maintaining muscle health and supporting various metabolic processes in the body."}{"title": "MSUD:MSUD, or Maple Syrup Urine Disease, is a metabolic disorder that impairs the body's ability to process specific amino acids. This condition necessitates careful dietary management to prevent complications and may require liver transplantation in severe cases."}{"title": "VITAFLO:Vitaflo is a company that produces specialized nutritional products for patients with metabolic disorders, including MSUD."}{"title": "LOPHELX LQ 20:Lophelx LQ 20 is a nutritional product designed for patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease."}{"title": "MSUD MAXAMAID:MSUD Maxamaid is a specialized formula for managing Maple Syrup Urine Disease."}{"title": "MSUD MAXAMUM:MSUD Maxamum is another specialized formula for patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease."}{"title": "TABLE 4:Table 4 outlines the protein and energy requirements for patients with MSUD according to Wappner and Gibson."}{"title": "TABLE 6:Table 6 provides a comprehensive overview of dietary treatment strategies during metabolic decompensations in patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD). Additionally, it outlines the fluid needs of children, utilizing the Holliday-Segar equation to determine appropriate hydration requirements. This table serves as a valuable resource for understanding both the nutritional management of MSUD and the fluid intake necessary for pediatric patients."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS CON PNAVB:Alimentos con PNAVB refers to foods that are high in branched-chain amino acids, which are restricted in the diet of patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDOS:Reci\u00e9n nacidos refers to newborns, for whom specific dietary protein and amino acid requirements are outlined in the treatment of MSUD."}{"title": "ESCOLARES:Escolares refers to school-aged children, with tailored dietary requirements for managing Maple Syrup Urine Disease."}{"title": "ADOLESCENTES Y ADULTOS:Adolescentes y adultos refers to teenagers and adults, with specific dietary guidelines for managing MSUD."}{"title": "HEPATIC TRANSPLANT:Hepatic transplant is a surgical procedure that may be considered for patients with classic MSUD to correct metabolic defects."}{"title": "PHENYLBUTYRATE:Phenylbutyrate is a therapeutic option being studied for MSUD, which can inhibit certain enzymes and help regulate amino acid levels."}{"title": "HOMOCYSTINURIA:Homocystinuria is a genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in cystathionine beta-synthase, which results in elevated levels of homocysteine in the blood. This condition is classified as an autosomal recessive disorder that affects methionine metabolism, leading to the accumulation of homocysteine and related compounds."}{"title": "IRELAND:Ireland is noted for having a higher prevalence of homocystinuria, occurring in approximately 1 in 200,000 to 335,000 live births."}{"title": "KCALIP:Kcalip is a brand that offers hypercaloric supplements for patients requiring dietary management."}{"title": "ENERGYVIT:Energyvit is a brand that provides hypercaloric supplements for dietary needs in medical conditions."}{"title": "CISTE\u00cdNA:Ciste\u00edna is a non-essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of homociste\u00edna and is often supplemented in dietary treatments."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MARFAN:S\u00edndrome de Marfan is a genetic disorder that shares clinical manifestations with elevated levels of homociste\u00edna, such as osteoporosis and skeletal abnormalities."}{"title": "CISTATIONINA:Cistationina is a compound involved in the metabolism of homociste\u00edna and is affected by dietary intake of amino acids."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO DIET\u00c9TICO-NUTRICIONAL:\"TRATAMIENTO DIET\u00c9TICO-NUTRICIONAL\" refers to dietary management strategies aimed at controlling protein intake and managing symptoms in patients with urea cycle disorders. This treatment also focuses on regulating levels of homocysteine and related amino acids in affected individuals. Through these dietary interventions, the goal is to improve the overall health and well-being of patients by addressing specific metabolic needs associated with these disorders."}{"title": "ACIDURIA METILMAL\u00d3NICA:Aciduria metilmal\u00f3nica is a metabolic condition that can occur alongside elevated homociste\u00edna levels, indicating a disruption in amino acid metabolism."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS INTRAVASCULAR:Trombosis intravascular is a potential clinical manifestation associated with high levels of homociste\u00edna, leading to blood clot formation."}{"title": "TROMBOEMBOLISMO:Tromboembolismo is a serious condition that can arise from elevated homociste\u00edna levels, resulting in blockages in blood vessels."}{"title": "RETRASO MENTAL:Retraso mental can be a consequence of metabolic disorders related to high homociste\u00edna levels, affecting cognitive development."}{"title": "ALTA HOMOCISTE\u00cdNA:"}{"title": "CYSTATHIONINE:Cystathionine is a compound involved in the metabolism of amino acids, particularly in the synthesis of cysteine and other related compounds."}{"title": "BETAINE:Betaine is a compound that can help lower homocysteine levels by acting as a methyl donor in the conversion of homocysteine to methionine."}{"title": "FOLATE:Folate is a B-vitamin necessary for DNA synthesis and repair, and it plays a role in the metabolism of homocysteine."}{"title": "UREA CYCLE DISORDERS:Urea cycle disorders are genetic conditions that result from deficiencies in enzymes that convert ammonia to urea, leading to toxic accumulation in the body."}{"title": "L-CYSTINE:L-Cystine is a compound that is essential for maintaining the synthesis of cystathionine and taurine, important for brain metabolism."}{"title": "CITRULLINE:Citrulline is an amino acid that can be administered to patients with certain urea cycle disorders to help manage ammonia levels."}{"title": "N-CARBAMYGLUTAMATE:N-carbamylglutamate is a treatment used for N-acetylglutamate synthase deficiency, a type of urea cycle disorder."}{"title": "GLYCINE:Glycine is the simplest amino acid and can accumulate in the body during metabolic disturbances, contributing to neurological symptoms."}{"title": "HYPERHOMOCYSTEINEMIA:Hyperhomocysteinemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of homocysteine in the blood, which can lead to various health issues, including cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "CYSTEINE:"}{"title": "N-ACETILGLUTAMATO SINTETASA:N-acetilglutamato sintetasa (NAGS) is an enzyme involved in the urea cycle, which helps in the metabolism of nitrogen in the body."}{"title": "CARBAMILFOSFATO SINTETASA:Carbamilfosfato sintetasa (CPS) is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, converting ammonia into urea."}{"title": "ORNIT\u00cdN TRANSACARBAMILASA:Ornit\u00edn transcarbamilasa (OTS) is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of carbamoyl phosphate and ornithine to citrulline in the urea cycle."}{"title": "ARGINOSUCCINATO SINTETASA:Arginosuccinato sintetasa (ASS) is an enzyme that facilitates the synthesis of argininosuccinate from citrulline and aspartate in the urea cycle."}{"title": "ARGINOSUCCINATO LIASA:Arginosuccinato liasa (ASL) is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of argininosuccinate to arginine and fumarate in the urea cycle."}{"title": "ARGINASA:Arginasa (ASA) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes arginine to ornithine and urea, playing a key role in the urea cycle."}{"title": "VITAFLO EAA:Vitaflo EAA is a dietary supplement specifically designed for the treatment of patients with urea cycle disorders, providing essential amino acids necessary for their health. It is particularly beneficial for individuals with severe metabolic disorders, including those suffering from carbamoyl phosphate synthetase (CPS) and ornithine transcarbamylase (OTC) deficiencies. This product plays a crucial role in amino acid supplementation, helping to manage the dietary needs of affected patients."}{"title": "UCD 1:UCD 1 is a specialized medical product designed for managing specific metabolic conditions, particularly those related to amino acid deficiencies. It serves as a dietary product specifically tailored for patients with urea cycle disorders, helping them to effectively manage their amino acid intake."}{"title": "UCD 2:UCD 2 is a dietary formulation specifically designed to support individuals with urea cycle disorders. This medical product aims to assist in the treatment of metabolic disorders that involve amino acids, providing essential nutritional support for those affected by these conditions."}{"title": "DIALAMINE:Dialamine is a nutritional product specifically designed for the management of urea cycle disorders. It provides essential amino acids that are crucial for patients with metabolic deficiencies. This formulation supports individuals who require supplementation of these vital nutrients to help maintain metabolic balance and overall health."}{"title": "ESSENTIAL AMINO ACID MIX:Essential Amino Acid Mix is a dietary supplement that provides essential amino acids for patients with urea cycle disorders."}{"title": "HIPOAMONIEMIA:Hipoamoniemia is the condition of having low levels of ammonia in the blood, which is a target state for managing urea cycle disorders."}{"title": "CETO\u00c1CIDOS:Ceto\u00e1cidos are organic acids that can be produced in the body and are relevant in the dietary management of patients with urea cycle disorders."}{"title": "HYPERTRANSAMINASEMIA:Hypertransaminasemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of transaminases in the blood. This condition can occur in patients with urea cycle disorders as well as in those with hepatic glycogenosis. The presence of elevated transaminases indicates potential liver dysfunction or other metabolic disturbances, highlighting the importance of monitoring these enzyme levels in affected individuals."}{"title": "ESSENTIAL AMINO ACIDMIX:Essential Amino AcidMix is a formulation used to supply essential amino acids to patients with metabolic disorders."}{"title": "N-CARBAMILGLUTAMATO:N-carbamylglutamate is a treatment used in patients with N-acetylglutamate synthase deficiency to activate CPS."}{"title": "HYPERAMONIEMIA:Hyperammonemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of ammonia in the blood, often requiring urgent treatment."}{"title": "OTC:OTC, or Ornithine Transcarbamylase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, which is essential for the detoxification of ammonia in the body. A deficiency in OTC can result in hyperammonemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of ammonia in the blood, which can be harmful. Additionally, OTC deficiency is associated with specific types of glycogen storage diseases, known as glucogenosis. This highlights the enzyme's importance not only in ammonia metabolism but also in broader metabolic processes."}{"title": "ASS:ASS (Argininosuccinate Synthetase) is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, which is essential for the metabolism of nitrogen in the body."}{"title": "ASL:ASL, or Argininosuccinate Lyase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle by facilitating the conversion of argininosuccinate into arginine and fumarate. A deficiency in ASL is linked to a specific type of glycogen storage disease, known as glucogenosis, highlighting its importance in metabolic processes."}{"title": "AMONIO:Ammonia is a toxic substance that can accumulate in the body due to metabolic disorders, leading to serious health issues."}{"title": "CPS:CPS, or Carbamoyl phosphate synthetase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle. Deficiencies in this enzyme are associated with glucogenosis, a condition that affects the metabolism of glycogen."}{"title": "GLUCOGENESIS:Glucogenesis is the process of glycogen synthesis, which can be affected in glucogenosis."}{"title": "TYPE I GLUCOGENOSIS:Type I glucogenosis, first described in 1929 by von Gierke, is characterized by hypoglycemia and hepatomegaly."}{"title": "VON GIERKE:Von Gierke was the discoverer of type I glucogenosis in 1929."}{"title": "AUTOSOMAL RECESSIVE:Most glucogenosis diseases are inherited in an autosomal recessive manner, except for certain types linked to the X chromosome."}{"title": "HEPATIC GLYCOGENOSIS:Hepatic glucogenosis refers to glycogen storage diseases that primarily affect the liver and are of nutritional interest."}{"title": "VALPROIC ACID:Valproic acid is a medication that should not be used for seizures in patients with glucogenosis as it decreases urea cycle activity."}{"title": "PHENOBARBITAL:Phenobarbital is another medication that is contraindicated in glucogenosis due to its effect on the urea cycle."}{"title": "HYPERAMMONEMIA:Hyperammonemia is a condition that can occur in patients with glucogenosis, requiring specific treatments."}{"title": "NEPHROMEGALY:Nephromegaly can be associated with glucogenosis and may present with proteinuria and renal insufficiency."}{"title": "METABOLIC ACIDOSIS:Metabolic acidosis can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in the context of hypoglycemia."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I:Glucogenosis de tipo I is a metabolic disorder characterized by the deficiency of the enzyme glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to hypoglycemia and lactic acidosis."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE VON GIERKE:Enfermedad de Von Gierke is a condition marked by the deficiency of glucose-6-phosphatase, resulting in the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and associated metabolic issues."}{"title": "BIOQU\u00cdMICO:Bioqu\u00edmico refers to the biochemical analysis performed to diagnose conditions like glucogenosis de tipo I and enfermedad de Von Gierke."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOSIS MUSCULAR:Glucogenosis muscular is a category of glycogen storage diseases that primarily affect muscle tissue, resulting in muscle-related symptoms."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOSIS GENERALIZADA:Glucogenosis generalizada encompasses glycogen storage diseases that affect multiple organs and systems in the body."}{"title": "BAJA ESTATURA:Baja estatura is a clinical symptom that can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in hepatic forms."}{"title": "HIPERLACTACIDEMIA:Hiperlactacidemia is a condition of elevated lactate levels in the blood, often seen in metabolic disorders like glucogenosis."}{"title": "CARDIOPAT\u00cdA:Cardiopat\u00eda refers to heart disease, which encompasses various conditions affecting the heart. In the context of glucogenosis, particularly the muscular forms, cardiopat\u00eda can manifest as a symptom. Additionally, it is noted that cardiopat\u00eda can also be caused by the accumulation of iron in the myocardium. Thus, cardiopat\u00eda is a broad term that includes heart diseases resulting from different underlying conditions, including metabolic disorders and iron overload."}{"title": "MIOTON\u00cdA:Mioton\u00eda is a condition characterized by delayed relaxation of muscles after contraction, which can occur in some muscular glucogenosis."}{"title": "ANEMIA HEMOL\u00cdTICA:Anemia hemol\u00edtica is a medical condition characterized by the accelerated destruction of red blood cells, resulting in a higher rate of red blood cell breakdown than their production. This condition can lead to elevated levels of \u00e1cido \u00farico in the body. Anemia hemol\u00edtica may also be associated with certain types of glucogenosis, which are metabolic disorders affecting glycogen storage and utilization."}{"title": "CONVULSIONES:Convulsiones are seizures that can occur in patients with certain types of glucogenosis, particularly those affecting the nervous system. Additionally, convulsiones can also manifest in severe cases of hyponatremia."}{"title": "BIOPSIA DE TEJIDO HEP\u00c1TICO:Biopsia de tejido hep\u00e1tico is a diagnostic procedure used to assess liver conditions, including glucogenosis.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CARDIOMIOPAT\u00cdA:Cardiomiopat\u00eda is a condition characterized by heart muscle disease, which can lead to heart failure and other complications."}{"title": "LAFLORA:Lafora is associated with a genetic condition known as Lafora disease, which involves a deficiency of laforin and leads to various neurological symptoms."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I:Glucogenosis tipo I is a metabolic disorder affecting the body's ability to break down glycogen, leading to various health complications."}{"title": "GLYCOSADE:Glycosade is a modified starch that helps maintain blood glucose levels during fasting periods, particularly useful for patients with metabolic disorders."}{"title": "VON GIERKE TYPE IA:Von Gierke Type Ia is a specific type of hepatic glycogen storage disease characterized by a deficiency in glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to severe hypoglycemia and other metabolic complications."}{"title": "GM-CSF:Granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF) is a cytokine used in the treatment of certain metabolic disorders to stimulate the production of white blood cells."}{"title": "G-CSF:Granulocyte colony-stimulating factor (G-CSF) is a cytokine that promotes the production of neutrophils and is used in the treatment of neutropenia in metabolic disorders."}{"title": "CALCIO Y VITAMINA D:Calcium and vitamin D are essential nutrients that may be beneficial as supplements in the treatment of hepatic glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "IECA:IECA, or angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, are medications recommended for patients experiencing microalbuminuria, particularly in the context of metabolic disorders. These medications play a crucial role in managing conditions associated with kidney function and protein excretion. Additionally, it has been noted that IECA may be associated with the occurrence of diarrhea as a side effect."}{"title": "PHENYLALANINE HYDROXYLASE DEFICIENCY:Phenylalanine hydroxylase deficiency is a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process phenylalanine, leading to various health issues if untreated."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF HUMAN GENETICS:The European Journal of Human Genetics publishes research related to human genetics, including studies on phenylketonuria."}{"title": "ARCHIVES OF DISEASE IN CHILDHOOD:Archives of Disease in Childhood is a journal that publishes research on childhood diseases, including dietary treatments for phenylketonuria."}{"title": "XI REUNI\u00d3N ASOCIACI\u00d3N DE NEUROCIENCIAS DEL DESARROLLO:The XI Reuni\u00f3n Asociaci\u00f3n de Neurociencias del Desarrollo is a meeting focused on developmental neuroscience, which may include discussions on metabolic disorders."}{"title": "MOLTHERAPY:Molecular Therapy is a journal that publishes research on gene therapy and related fields, including treatments for metabolic disorders."}{"title": "HUMAN MUTATION:Human Mutation is a journal that publishes research on genetic mutations and their implications, including those related to phenylketonuria."}{"title": "GENETIC METABOLISM:Genetic Metabolism is a journal that focuses on metabolic disorders and their genetic underpinnings, including phenylketonuria."}{"title": "SODIUM PHENYLBUTYRATE:Sodium phenylbutyrate is a drug used to treat urea cycle disorders, which may be relevant in the context of metabolic disorders like phenylketonuria."}{"title": "CADIZ:C\u00e1diz is a city in Spain where the XI Reuni\u00f3n Asociaci\u00f3n de Neurociencias del Desarrollo took place."}{"title": "MAY 2013:May 2013 is the date when the XI Reuni\u00f3n Asociaci\u00f3n de Neurociencias del Desarrollo was held."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF BIOLOGICAL CHEMISTRY:The Journal of Biological Chemistry publishes research on biochemical processes, including studies related to metabolic disorders."}{"title": "OMIM:OMIM (Online Mendelian Inheritance in Man) is a comprehensive and authoritative compendium that serves as a database of human genes and genetic disorders. It includes detailed information on various genetic conditions, such as homocystinuria and phenylketonuria, making it a vital resource for researchers and healthcare professionals interested in genetics."}{"title": "IONINE B-SYNTHASE:Ionine b-synthase is an enzyme involved in the metabolism of homocysteine and is linked to homocystinuria causing mutations."}{"title": "NATIONAL UREA CYCLE DISORDERS FOUNDATION:The National Urea Cycle Disorders Foundation is an organization dedicated to providing information and support for individuals with urea cycle disorders."}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ENFERMOS DE GLUCOGENOSIS:The Asociaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Enfermos de Glucogenosis is a Spanish association that supports individuals affected by glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "GENE REVIEWS:Gene Reviews is a comprehensive resource that provides information on genetic conditions, including homocystinuria and glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF PEDIATRICS:The European Journal of Pediatrics is a scholarly publication that focuses on various aspects of pediatric health. It publishes a wide range of research and articles, including those related to nutrition and reviews on pediatric health. Additionally, the journal features studies on metabolic disorders, such as glycogen storage diseases, contributing to the understanding and advancement of pediatric medicine."}{"title": "MOLECULAR GENETICS AND METABOLISM:Molecular Genetics and Metabolism is a journal that focuses on the genetic basis of metabolic disorders, including glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "CYSTATHIONINE BETA-SYNTHASE:"}{"title": "MIGUEL A. RUBIO:Miguel A. Rubio is a clinical nutritionist affiliated with the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario San Carlos, focusing on dietary impacts on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "CARMEN MORENO:Carmen Moreno is a healthcare professional working in primary care at Centro de Salud Lucero in Madrid."}{"title": "DRA. M.\u00aa NURIA VIRGILI CASAS:Dra. M.\u00aa Nuria Virgili Casas is a medical professional specializing in lipid disorders and their dietary management."}{"title": "DRA. PERE LEYES I GARC\u00cdA:Dra. Pere Leyes i Garc\u00eda is a medical professional focusing on ketogenic diets and their effects on health."}{"title": "JOAN TRABAL V\u00cdLCHEZ:Joan Trabal V\u00edlchez is a Dietitian-Nutritionist at Hospital Cl\u00ednic, where he specializes in clinical nutrition and dietary therapy. He is particularly involved in dietary therapies for epilepsy, applying his expertise to support patients with this condition through tailored nutritional interventions."}{"title": "TRIGLIC\u00c9RIDOS DE CADENA LARGA Y CADENA MEDIA:Long-chain and medium-chain triglycerides are types of fats that are significant in dietary management for certain medical conditions."}{"title": "DRA. ROSA BURGOS PEL\u00c1EZ:"}{"title": "GRASA SATURADA:GRASA SATURADA refers to saturated fat, a type of fat that can significantly impact cardiovascular health and is frequently discussed in dietary studies. This type of fat is primarily found in animal-based foods and tropical oils. It is associated with an increase in cholesterol levels and a heightened risk of cardiovascular diseases (ECV). Research indicates that replacing saturated fat with monounsaturated fatty acids can lead to a reduction in LDL cholesterol, suggesting that dietary choices regarding fat types can influence heart health."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS DE CADENA LARGA:Los \u00e1cidos grasos saturados de cadena larga son un tipo de grasa que se asocia con un mayor riesgo de arteriosclerosis y ECV."}{"title": "ACEITE DE PALMA:El aceite de palma es un tipo de grasa que contiene una mayor proporci\u00f3n de \u00e1cidos grasos saturados de cadena larga, lo que lo relaciona con el riesgo de ECV."}{"title": "FITOESTEROLES:Fitoesteroles, also known as phytosterols, are plant-derived compounds recognized for their potential health benefits, particularly in relation to cardiovascular health. They are known to aid in reducing cholesterol levels by decreasing cholesterol absorption in the intestines, which can lead to lower levels of LDL cholesterol. This dual action of helping to reduce overall cholesterol and improving heart health makes fitoesteroles a valuable component in dietary strategies aimed at promoting cardiovascular well-being."}{"title": "FIBRA SOLUBLE:La fibra soluble es un tipo de fibra que puede influir positivamente en la salud cardiovascular."}{"title": "VITAMINAS ANTIOXIDANTES:Las vitaminas antioxidantes son nutrientes que ayudan a combatir el estr\u00e9s oxidativo y pueden mejorar la salud cardiovascular."}{"title": "AGS:AGS refers to saturated fatty acids, which are discussed in the context of their impact on cholesterol levels and cardiovascular disease risk."}{"title": "ECV:ECV, which stands for cardiovascular disease, is a health condition that is being analyzed in relation to dietary fats. Additionally, ECV refers to cerebrovascular disease (Enfermedad Cerebrovascular), which is an acute process that can benefit from appropriate nutritional management."}{"title": "AGPI:AGPI, or Acidos Grasos Poliinsaturados, refers to polyunsaturated fatty acids that play a significant role in health by reducing inflammation and enhancing muscle response. These fatty acids are recommended as substitutes for saturated fats, contributing to lower cholesterol levels and promoting overall cardiovascular health."}{"title": "AGM:AGM refers to monounsaturated fatty acids, which are recognized as healthier dietary options compared to saturated fats. These fatty acids are considered beneficial for heart health and play a significant role in the Mediterranean diet. Monounsaturated fatty acids (AGM) are healthy fats found in foods such as olive oil and nuts, contributing to overall well-being."}{"title": "GSAT:GSAT refers to saturated fatty acids, which are being studied for their association with coronary heart disease."}{"title": "ACEITE COLZA:A type of oil with 6.6% saturated fats, 57.2% monounsaturated fats, and 31.5% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE CANOLA:A type of oil containing 7.1% saturated fats, 58.9% monounsaturated fats, and 29.6% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE MA\u00cdZ:A type of oil with 12.7% saturated fats, 24.2% monounsaturated fats, and 58.7% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE GIRASOL:A type of oil that contains 13.1% saturated fats, 31.8% monounsaturated fats, and 50% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE SOJA:A type of oil containing 14.4% saturated fats, 23.3% monounsaturated fats, and 57.9% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE CACAHUETE:A type of oil with 16.9% saturated fats, 46.2% monounsaturated fats, and 32% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "MARGARINA:Margarina is a type of fat spread that consists of 18% saturated fats, 48% monounsaturated fats, and 29% polyunsaturated fats. It is commonly used in cooking and baking. However, it is recommended that its consumption be limited in children's diets due to health considerations. Additionally, Margarina can be included in modified diets under specific conditions, indicating its versatility in various dietary plans."}{"title": "ACEITE SALM\u00d3N:A type of oil with 19.8% saturated fats, 29% monounsaturated fats, and 40.3% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE H\u00cdGADO BACALAO:A type of oil containing 22.6% saturated fats, 46.7% monounsaturated fats, and 22.5% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "GRASA PAVO:A type of fat with 29.4% saturated fats, 42.9% monounsaturated fats, and 23.1% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "GRASA POLLO:A type of fat containing 29.8% saturated fats, 44.7% monounsaturated fats, and 20.9% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "TOCINO:A type of fat with 39.2% saturated fats, 45.1% monounsaturated fats, and 11.2% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "GRASA CORDERO:A type of fat containing 47.3% saturated fats, 40.6% monounsaturated fats, and 7.8% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "GRASA VACUNO:A type of fat with 49.8% saturated fats, 41.8% monounsaturated fats, and 4.2% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE PALMA:A type of oil containing 49.3% saturated fats, 37% monounsaturated fats, and 9.3% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "MANTECA CACAO:A type of fat containing 59.7% saturated fats, 32.9% monounsaturated fats, and 3% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE PALMISTE:A type of oil with 81.5% saturated fats, 11.4% monounsaturated fats, and 1.6% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "ACEITE COCO:A type of oil containing 86.5% saturated fats, 5.8% monounsaturated fats, and 1.8% polyunsaturated fats."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA:\u00c1cidos Grasos de Cadena Corta, or short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), are a type of fatty acid characterized by having one to six carbon atoms. They are primarily produced through the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates and dietary fibers in the colon. These fatty acids play a crucial role in various physiological processes and are absorbed by the colon. Notably, SCFAs have no effect on atherogenesis and thrombogenesis, indicating their neutral impact on certain cardiovascular conditions. Overall, \u00c1cidos Grasos de Cadena Corta are important metabolites that contribute to gut health and metabolic functions."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO L\u00c1URICO:A type of fatty acid with a positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO MIR\u00cdSTICO:A type of fatty acid with a strong positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO PALM\u00cdTICO:A type of fatty acid with a moderate positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO ESTE\u00c1RICO:A type of fatty acid with a neutral to positive effect on atherogenesis and a positive effect on thrombogenesis."}{"title": "EPIC-NL:The European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition-Netherlands is a cohort study that evaluates the relationship between diet and health outcomes, including cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "GRASA TRANS:Grasa trans refers to trans fat, which is associated with increased risk of cardiovascular disease and is a focus of dietary recommendations."}{"title": "METAN\u00c1LISIS:METAN\u00c1LISIS es un estudio que utiliza una t\u00e9cnica estad\u00edstica para combinar los resultados de m\u00faltiples investigaciones, con el objetivo de mejorar la potencia y precisi\u00f3n de los hallazgos. Este enfoque es especialmente \u00fatil en el \u00e1mbito de la nutrici\u00f3n, donde se busca obtener conclusiones m\u00e1s precisas y significativas sobre la eficacia de diferentes dietas. En particular, el metan\u00e1lisis se ha utilizado para evaluar la eficacia de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica en comparaci\u00f3n con la dieta Atkins modificada, as\u00ed como para obtener conclusiones m\u00e1s robustas sobre la relaci\u00f3n entre la dieta y los resultados de salud. En resumen, el metan\u00e1lisis es una herramienta valiosa que permite sintetizar informaci\u00f3n de diversos estudios para ofrecer una visi\u00f3n m\u00e1s clara y fundamentada sobre temas espec\u00edficos en la investigaci\u00f3n cient\u00edfica."}{"title": "CANCER Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:Cancer y nutrici\u00f3n refers to the relationship between dietary intake and cancer risk, which is a focus of epidemiological studies."}{"title": "METAN\u00c1LISIS DE ESTUDIOS EPIDEMIOL\u00d3GICOS:Metan\u00e1lisis de estudios epidemiol\u00f3gicos are comprehensive analyses that evaluate the relationship between diet and health outcomes, including cardiovascular disease and cancer."}{"title": "SOCIETY EUROPEA DE CARDIOLOG\u00cdA:The European Society of Cardiology issues recommendations for dietary fat intake, suggesting even lower saturated fat consumption between 5-6%."}{"title": "BIOMARCADORES:Biomarkers are indicators used in epidemiological studies to assess the intake of saturated fats and their association with cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "GRASAS INSATURADAS:Unsaturated fats are considered healthier alternatives to saturated and trans fats and are recommended for reducing cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "AGT:"}{"title": "ACEITE DE OLIVA VIRGEN:Extra virgin olive oil is a key component of the Mediterranean diet, recommended for its health benefits, particularly in cardiovascular health."}{"title": "CRETA:Creta is an island in Greece renowned for its traditional Mediterranean diet, which is linked to lower rates of coronary heart disease. The island's dietary habits, characterized by a high intake of alpha-linolenic acid (ALA), contribute to its notably low rates of coronary disease. This combination of dietary practices and health outcomes highlights Creta's significance in discussions about nutrition and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "AGP:AGP refers to polyunsaturated fatty acids, which are essential fats that play a crucial role in cardiovascular health."}{"title": "RIESGO DE ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA:Risk of coronary disease refers to the likelihood of developing heart-related conditions, influenced by dietary intake and lifestyle."}{"title": "LYON HEART STUDY:The Lyon Heart Study is an intervention study that demonstrated a significant reduction in mortality among participants consuming ALA."}{"title": "AGP \u03a9-6:AGP \u03c9-6 refers to omega-6 fatty acids that are recommended for cholesterol reduction when replacing saturated fats in the diet."}{"title": "AGP \u03a9-3:AGP \u03c9-3 refers to omega-3 fatty acids, including EPA and DHA, which are important for cardiovascular health."}{"title": "GISSI-PREVENZIONE TRIAL:The GISSI-Prevenzione Trial is a clinical study that investigated the effects of dietary supplementation with n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids, specifically eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA), along with vitamin E, in patients who had experienced a myocardial infarction. The trial demonstrated a significant reduction in coronary mortality among those patients who received the supplementation, highlighting the potential benefits of these nutrients in post-myocardial infarction care."}{"title": "ESTUDIO JELIS:The JELIS study is a clinical trial that demonstrated a reduction in ischemic events among patients treated with EPA in addition to statins."}{"title": "OMEGA:The OMEGA study is a clinical trial that investigated the effects of EPA and DHA on patients with a history of myocardial infarction."}{"title": "ALPHA-OMEGA:The ALPHA-OMEGA study is a clinical trial that assessed the impact of EPA and DHA on patients with a history of myocardial infarction."}{"title": "SU.FOL.OM3:The SU.FOL.OM3 study is a clinical trial that evaluated the effects of omega-3 fatty acids on patients with recent ischemic events."}{"title": "HIPOLESTEROLEMIA:Hipocholesterolemia refers to the condition of having low cholesterol levels, which can be influenced by dietary intake of omega-6 fatty acids."}{"title": "RISK AND PREVENTION STUDY COLLABORATIVE GROUP:The Risk and Prevention Study Collaborative Group conducted a study involving 12,513 patients with multiple cardiovascular risk factors to assess the effects of EPA+DHA on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality."}{"title": "EPA+DHA:EPA+DHA refers to eicosapentaenoic acid and docosahexaenoic acid, which are omega-3 fatty acids studied for their effects on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "AGP-\u03a93:AGP-\u03c93 refers to omega-3 fatty acids derived from fish, which are evaluated for their protective effects against coronary disease and sudden death."}{"title": "ISQUEMIA CEREBRAL:Isquemia cerebral refers to a condition where there is insufficient blood flow to the brain, potentially resulting in a stroke."}{"title": "MORBIMORTALIDAD CARDIOVASCULAR:Morbimortalidad cardiovascular refers to the incidence of morbidity and mortality associated with cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "ANTIGREGANTES PLAQUETARIOS:Antigregantes plaquetarios are medications that prevent blood clots by inhibiting platelet aggregation, used in cardiovascular disease management."}{"title": "MUERTE S\u00daBITA:Muerte s\u00fabita refers to sudden death, often associated with cardiac events."}{"title": "REINFARTO MORTAL:Reinfarto mortal refers to a fatal heart attack, which can occur after a previous heart attack."}{"title": "ISQUEMIA CORONARIA:"}{"title": "HEALTH PROFESSIONALS FOLLOW-UP STUDY:The Health Professionals Follow-up Study is a long-term epidemiological study that has provided valuable information on the association between food consumption and diseases over 26 years."}{"title": "\u03a9-3:\u03c9-3 fatty acids are essential fats that the body cannot produce by itself, important for heart and brain health."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS \u03a9-3:\u00c1cidos \u03c9-3 are essential fatty acids important for heart and brain health, derived from fish and other sources."}{"title": "VERDOLAGA:Verdolaga is a plant that contains omega-3 fatty acids and is suggested for dietary inclusion."}{"title": "BORRAJA:Borraja is a plant known for its omega-3 fatty acid content, beneficial for health."}{"title": "SEMILLAS DE LINO:Semillas de lino, or flaxseeds, are a rich source of omega-3 fatty acids and are recommended for consumption."}{"title": "EMBARAZADAS:Embarazadas refers to pregnant women who are advised to avoid certain fish due to mercury content."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS PEQUE\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os peque\u00f1os refers to young children who are advised to limit fish consumption due to mercury exposure."}{"title": "C\u00c1PSULAS DE \u03a9-3:C\u00e1psulas de \u03c9-3 are supplements containing omega-3 fatty acids, recommended for various populations."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS ANIMALES:Alimentos animales refer to animal-based foods that contain dietary cholesterol, impacting cardiovascular health."}{"title": "ESTEROL VEGETAL:Esterol vegetal refers to plant sterols that can influence lipid levels and cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "ESTANOL:Estanol refers to plant-derived compounds that can help manage cholesterol levels."}{"title": "L\u00cdPIDOS PLASM\u00c1TICOS:L\u00edpidos plasm\u00e1ticos refer to lipids in the blood that are influenced by diet and can affect cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "EFECTOS POSITIVOS:Efectos positivos refer to the beneficial impacts of omega-3 fatty acids on health."}{"title": "CONTAMINANTES AMBIENTALES:Contaminantes ambientales refer to environmental pollutants that can affect health, particularly in relation to omega-3 fatty acids.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "AHA/ACC:The American Heart Association and American College of Cardiology provide guidelines for cardiovascular health and dietary recommendations."}{"title": "DASH:DASH, which stands for Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension, is a dietary model specifically designed to control and manage blood pressure through targeted food consumption. This dietary plan emphasizes the importance of increasing the intake of fruits and vegetables, which are rich in essential nutrients, including calcium. The DASH diet is recommended not only for preventing hypertension but also for improving overall health. Research from the DASH study indicates that adhering to a diet rich in these food groups can lead to beneficial effects on blood pressure, making it an effective approach for those looking to manage hypertension through nutritional changes."}{"title": "OMNIHEART:The OmniHeart study introduced three dietary variations aimed at optimizing macronutrient intake for heart health."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS INTEGRALES:Whole grains are recommended in dietary guidelines to promote cardiovascular health and are included in both DASH and Mediterranean diets."}{"title": "L\u00c1CTEOS BAJOS EN GRASAS:Low-fat dairy products are part of the DASH diet and Mediterranean diet, contributing to a heart-healthy eating pattern."}{"title": "CARNES MAGRAS:CARNES MAGRAS, or lean meats, are defined as cuts of meat that contain less fat. Research indicates that these meats have a neutral effect on cardiovascular risk, making them a beneficial choice for heart health. They are included in dietary recommendations, particularly in the DASH (Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension) diet, which promotes heart health. Additionally, lean meats are permitted in modified diets and are recommended as a protein source in children's diets, highlighting their versatility and nutritional value."}{"title": "VEGAN DIET:A vegan diet that excludes all animal products, focusing solely on plant-based foods, which may have cardiovascular benefits."}{"title": "AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION (AHA):The AHA is a non-profit organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for cardiovascular health, including dietary advice."}{"title": "HYPOGLYCEMIC INDEX:A measure that ranks foods based on their effect on blood sugar levels, which is relevant in dietary recommendations for preventing obesity and diabetes."}{"title": "FITOQU\u00cdMICOS:Bioactive compounds found in plants that may have health benefits, particularly in relation to cardiovascular health."}{"title": "NUTS:Nuts are a significant component of dietary recommendations due to their nutritional profile, particularly their phosphorus content, which has implications for renal patients. They are recognized for being high in healthy fats and essential nutrients, contributing to a lower risk of cardiovascular diseases when incorporated into a balanced diet."}{"title": "ADDED SUGARS:Added sugars are sugars that are incorporated into foods and beverages, which can contribute to obesity and cardiovascular disease when consumed in high amounts."}{"title": "ACEITE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA:El aceite de oliva virgen extra es un tipo de aceite vegetal que se ha asociado con beneficios para la salud cardiovascular, especialmente en la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea."}{"title": "CARNES PROCESADAS:CARNES PROCESADAS se refiere a productos c\u00e1rnicos que han sido modificados con el fin de mejorar su conservaci\u00f3n y sabor. Sin embargo, el consumo de carnes procesadas ha sido objeto de preocupaci\u00f3n debido a su asociaci\u00f3n con un mayor riesgo cardiovascular. Adem\u00e1s, se ha discutido su posible v\u00ednculo con el c\u00e1ncer en el contexto de las recomendaciones diet\u00e9ticas. Estas consideraciones resaltan la importancia de evaluar el consumo de carnes procesadas en la dieta, dado su impacto potencial en la salud."}{"title": "LACTEOS:LACTEOS refers to dairy products, which include items such as milk, cheese, and yogurt. These products are considered neutral in their effect on cardiovascular risk. They are recommended for patients, with a suggested intake of one serving per day, preferably in a semi-skimmed form. Additionally, LACTEOS have a high phosphorus to protein ratio, which necessitates monitoring in patients with hyperphosphatemia and chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD ECV:La mortalidad por enfermedad cardiovascular (ECV) se refiere a las muertes causadas por condiciones cardiovasculares, y se relaciona con factores de riesgo como la dieta."}{"title": "SOY PROTEIN:Soy protein is recognized for its health benefits, including its antioxidant properties and role in reducing cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "FRUITS AND VEGETABLES:Fruits and vegetables are recommended for their high content of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants that promote heart health."}{"title": "CAROTENOS:Carotenoids are pigments found in fruits and vegetables that have antioxidant properties and may influence health."}{"title": "ENSALADAS:Ensaladas are salads made from various vegetables and fruits, often consumed for their health benefits."}{"title": "AGUACATES:Aguacates are avocados, rich in healthy fats and nutrients, commonly used in various dishes."}{"title": "DATILES:Datiles, also known as dates, are a sweet fruit that is high in fiber and nutrients. They provide 2 mg of iron per 100 grams, making them a nutritious addition to the diet. Often used in desserts, datiles are appreciated for their natural sweetness and health benefits."}{"title": "HIGOS SECOS:Higos secos are dried figs, recognized for their natural sweetness and numerous health benefits. They are classified as a type of dried fruit and are recommended as part of a low-sodium diet, highlighting their nutritional value and versatility in various dietary plans."}{"title": "CIRUELAS SECAS:CIRUELAS SECAS, known as prunes, are a type of dried fruit that are often consumed for their digestive benefits. They are also recommended as part of a low-sodium diet, highlighting their nutritional value and versatility in various dietary plans."}{"title": "PASAS:Pasas are raisins, dried grapes that are high in sugar and nutrients."}{"title": "PATATAS CONGELADAS PRECOCINADAS:Patatas congeladas precocinadas are frozen pre-cooked potatoes, convenient for quick meals."}{"title": "CASTA\u00d1AS:Casta\u00f1as are chestnuts, a type of nut that is often roasted and consumed as a snack."}{"title": "AVELLANAS:Avellanas are hazelnuts, often used in desserts and known for their flavor."}{"title": "PI\u00d1ONES:Pi\u00f1ones, also known as pine nuts, are a type of dry fruit that is recognized for its rich flavor and culinary versatility. They are often recommended as part of a hypocaloric diet due to their nutritional benefits. These nuts are commonly used in various cooking applications, enhancing dishes with their distinctive taste."}{"title": "PEPITAS GIRASOL:Pepitas girasol are sunflower seeds, often used as a snack or in salads."}{"title": "S\u00c9SAMO:S\u00e9samo refers to sesame seeds, which are used in various cuisines and known for their health benefits."}{"title": "MANTEQUILLA DE CACAHUETE:Mantequilla de cacahuete is peanut butter, a popular spread known for its protein content."}{"title": "MARISCOS:Mariscos refers to seafood, which includes various types of fish and shellfish."}{"title": "SARDINAS:Sardinas, commonly known as sardines, are a type of fish that are often canned and consumed for their numerous health benefits. They provide a significant nutritional value, offering 3.2 mg of iron per 100 grams. Additionally, sardinas are rich in purines, which can influence uric acid levels in the body. This combination of nutritional benefits and potential health considerations makes sardinas a noteworthy choice in a balanced diet."}{"title": "ANGUILA:Anguila is eel, a type of fish that is often used in various cuisines."}{"title": "GAMBAS:Gambas are shrimp, a popular seafood known for its flavor and versatility in cooking."}{"title": "LANGOSTINOS:Langostinos are prawns, often used in various dishes and known for their taste."}{"title": "CAVIAR:Caviar is fish eggs, considered a delicacy and often associated with luxury."}{"title": "HUEVAS DE PESCADO:Huevas de pescado are fish roe, often used in various culinary applications."}{"title": "MOJAMA:Mojama is a type of cured fish that is often consumed as a delicacy. However, it is important to note that dried fish, including mojama, is not allowed in the modified diet."}{"title": "MARGARINAS VEGETALES:Margarinas vegetales are vegetable margarines, often used as a butter substitute."}{"title": "ACEITE DE CACAHUETE:Aceite de cacahuete is peanut oil, commonly used in cooking for its flavor."}{"title": "MANTEQUILLAS:Mantequillas refers to butters, which are used in cooking and baking."}{"title": "ACEITES HIDROGENADOS:Aceites hidrogenados are hydrogenated oils, often used in processed foods."}{"title": "GRASAS VEGETALES:Grasas vegetales are vegetable fats, used in cooking and food production."}{"title": "POSTRES:Postres refers to desserts, which are sweet dishes typically served at the end of a meal."}{"title": "REPOSTER\u00cdA:Reposter\u00eda refers to pastry and baking, encompassing various sweet baked goods."}{"title": "JALEAS:Jaleas are jellies, sweet spreads made from fruit juice and sugar."}{"title": "TURR\u00d3N:Turr\u00f3n is a type of nougat, a traditional sweet made from nuts and honey."}{"title": "MAZAP\u00c1N:Mazap\u00e1n is marzipan, a sweet made from almond paste and sugar."}{"title": "FRUTAS EN ALM\u00cdBAR:Frutas en alm\u00edbar are fruits preserved in syrup, often used in desserts."}{"title": "ATP-III:ATP-III refers to the Adult Treatment Panel III, which provides guidelines for the treatment of cardiovascular diseases and dietary recommendations."}{"title": "GAZPACHO:Gazpacho is a traditional Spanish cold soup that has been associated with improved blood pressure control in dietary studies."}{"title": "NUTRICIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS:Nutritional recommendations refer to guidelines provided for dietary intake to promote health and prevent diseases, particularly cardiovascular issues."}{"title": "BEBIDAS ALCOH\u00d3LICAS:Alcoholic beverages are mentioned in dietary guidelines with recommendations for limited consumption."}{"title": "KEYS A:Keys A is an author known for his work on coronary heart disease, particularly in the context of dietary influences, as published in the journal Circulation."}{"title": "GRUNDY SM:Grundy SM is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of dietary fats and their impact on cardiovascular health. His work focuses on the dietary influences on serum lipids and lipoproteins, highlighting the critical relationship between nutrition and heart health. Through his research, Grundy SM has advanced the understanding of how dietary choices can affect lipid profiles and overall cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "MENSINK RP:Mensink RP is an author who has conducted meta-analyses on the effects of dietary fatty acids on serum lipids and lipoproteins."}{"title": "ROS E:Ros E is an author recognized for her contributions to the understanding of dietary influences on health. She has discussed the impact of dietary cholesterol on cholesterol levels and cardiovascular risk, providing valuable insights into how diet can affect heart health. Additionally, Ros E has played a significant role in establishing a consensus on the consumption of fats and oils in the diet specifically for the Spanish adult population, highlighting her expertise in nutritional guidelines and public health."}{"title": "SIRI-TARINO PW:Siri-Tarino PW is an author known for conducting meta-analyses on the association of saturated fat with cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "CHOWDHURY R:Chowdhury R is an author who has researched the association of dietary fatty acids with coronary risk."}{"title": "SCHAEFER EJ:"}{"title": "EUROPEAN ASSOCIATION FOR CARDIOVASCULAR PREVENTION & REHABILITATION:The European Association for Cardiovascular Prevention & Rehabilitation is a professional organization that focuses on the prevention and rehabilitation of cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION:The Journal of Clinical Nutrition is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on nutrition and its impact on health."}{"title": "NUTRITION METABOLISM AND CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE:Nutrition Metabolism and Cardiovascular Disease is a journal dedicated to exploring the intricate relationship between nutrition and cardiovascular health. It publishes research findings that highlight various aspects of this connection, including studies on the association between polyphenol intake and cardiovascular events. The journal serves as a valuable resource for understanding how dietary factors influence cardiovascular conditions and overall metabolic health."}{"title": "SEVEN COUNTRIES STUDY:The Seven Countries Study is a long-term epidemiological study that investigates the relationship between diet and cardiovascular disease across seven countries."}{"title": "EURAMIC STUDY:The EURAMIC study is a research project that examines the relationship between trans fatty acids and the risk of myocardial infarction in multiple countries."}{"title": "ZUTPHEN ELDERLY STUDY:The Zutphen Elderly Study is a prospective population-based research initiative that focuses on examining the relationship between dietary factors, particularly trans fatty acid intake, and the risk of coronary heart disease among elderly populations. Conducted over a 10-year period, the study aims to provide insights into how various dietary components influence heart health in older adults."}{"title": "HAFEKOST K:Hafekost K is a researcher who contributed to the meta-analysis on food sources of saturated fat and mortality."}{"title": "MITROU F:Mitrou F is an author of the study examining the association between saturated fat sources and mortality."}{"title": "MICA R:Micha R is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on red and processed meat consumption and its health risks."}{"title": "DAWCZYNSKI C:Dawczynski C is an author who studied the effects of saturated fatty acids on heart disease."}{"title": "HOOPER L:Hooper L is a researcher who reviewed the reduction of saturated fat intake for cardiovascular disease prevention."}{"title": "PIEPOLI MF:Piepoli MF is an author of the 2016 European Guidelines on cardiovascular disease prevention."}{"title": "KATAN MB:Katan MB is a researcher who studied the effects of trans fatty acids on lipoproteins."}{"title": "ZOCK PL:Zock PL is an author who researched the impact of dietary trans fatty acids on cholesterol levels."}{"title": "O'SULLIVAN TA:"}{"title": "JOURNAL OF LIPID RESEARCH:The Journal of Lipid Research published a comparison of dietary fatty acids and their effects on plasma lipids."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF THE AMERICAN COLLEGE OF CARDIOLOGY:This journal published a meta-analysis on the effect of the Mediterranean diet on metabolic syndrome."}{"title": "ANNALS OF INTERNAL MEDICINE:The \"Annals of Internal Medicine\" is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research and reviews related to various topics in internal medicine. It has published studies on conditions such as pagophagia and iron deficiency anemia, as well as hyponatremia. Additionally, the journal has featured a subgroup analysis of a randomized trial investigating the prevention of diabetes through Mediterranean diets. Through its diverse range of articles, the \"Annals of Internal Medicine\" contributes significantly to the field of internal medicine by disseminating important findings and insights."}{"title": "BMC MEDICINE:BMC Medicine published studies on olive oil intake and its association with cardiovascular disease and mortality."}{"title": "HU FB:Hu FB is a researcher actively engaged in various studies focusing on dietary patterns and their impact on cardiovascular health. Notably, Hu FB is involved in the PREDIMED trial, which investigates the effects of Mediterranean diets on cardiovascular disease. Additionally, Hu FB has authored a prospective study examining the relationship between egg consumption and the risk of cardiovascular disease. Through these contributions, Hu FB plays a significant role in advancing the understanding of nutrition and its effects on heart health."}{"title": "MANSON JE:Manson JE is a researcher who co-authored the study on dietary fat intake and risk of type 2 diabetes in women."}{"title": "STAMPFER MJ:Stampfer MJ is a prominent researcher known for his contributions to the field of nutrition and health. He is a co-author of a study that investigates the relationship between nutritional factors and hypertension among women in the United States. Additionally, Stampfer MJ has played a significant role in research focused on dietary fat intake and its effects on overall health. His work highlights the importance of dietary choices in managing health outcomes, particularly in relation to hypertension and other health conditions."}{"title": "MATTSON FH:Mattson FH is a researcher who compared the effects of different dietary fatty acids on plasma lipids."}{"title": "KASTORINI CM:Kastorini CM is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome."}{"title": "MILIONIS HJ:Milionis HJ is a researcher involved in the study of the Mediterranean diet's effects on health."}{"title": "NORDMANN AJ:Nordmann AJ is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis comparing Mediterranean and low-fat diets."}{"title": "SOFI F:Sofi F is a researcher known for her contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly through her systematic reviews on the benefits of the Mediterranean diet. She has also authored a meta-analysis that examines the relationship between the Mediterranean diet and health status, further solidifying her expertise in this area."}{"title": "ABBATE R:Abbate R is a researcher who co-authored a systematic review on the Mediterranean diet's health benefits."}{"title": "GENSINI GF:Gensini GF is a researcher known for his work on the Mediterranean diet and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "MARTINEZ-GONZALEZ MA:Martinez-Gonzalez MA is a researcher who has studied dietary patterns and their effects on cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "COVAS MI:Covas MI is a researcher involved in studies on the Mediterranean diet and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "CORELLA D:Corella D is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dietary patterns and health outcomes."}{"title": "AROS F:Aros F is a researcher who participated in the PREDIMED trial on the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "DOM\u00c9NECH M:Dom\u00e9nech M is a researcher who studied the effects of the Mediterranean diet on blood pressure and metabolic factors."}{"title": "ROMAN P:Roman P is a researcher who focuses on the health effects of the Mediterranean diet. In addition to this work, he is also an author who has contributed to research concerning malnutrition in outpatients with stable chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Through his diverse research interests, Roman P addresses important health issues related to diet and chronic illness."}{"title": "LAPETRA J:Lapetra J is a researcher who contributed to the clinical trial on the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "GUASCH-FERR\u00c9 M:Guasch-Ferr\u00e9 M is a researcher who studied olive oil intake and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "TRESSERRA-RIMBAU A:Tresserra-Rimbau A is a researcher who investigated the association between polyphenol intake and cardiovascular events."}{"title": "BURDGE G:Burdge G is a researcher who studied alpha-linolenic acid metabolism and its implications for health."}{"title": "DE LORGERIL M:De Lorgeril M is a researcher known for his work on the Mediterranean diet in secondary prevention of coronary heart disease.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "DE LORGERIL:De Lorgeril is a researcher involved in studies related to dietary fats and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "LYON DIET HEART STUDY:The Lyon Diet Heart Study is a clinical trial that investigated the effects of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular complications after myocardial infarction."}{"title": "OMEGA TRIAL:The OMEGA trial tested the effect of highly purified omega-3 fatty acids on patients after myocardial infarction."}{"title": "ALPHA-LINOLENIC ACID:Alpha-linolenic acid is an essential omega-3 fatty acid that plays a crucial role in cardiovascular health and is a key component of the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "N-3 FATTY ACIDS:N-3 fatty acids, including EPA and DHA, are essential fats that have been shown to benefit cardiovascular health and are often derived from fish oil."}{"title": "EICOSAPENTAENOIC ACID:Eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) is an omega-3 fatty acid that is important for cardiovascular health and is commonly found in fish oil."}{"title": "DOCOSAHEXAENOIC ACID:Docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) is an omega-3 fatty acid crucial for brain and heart health, often studied in dietary research."}{"title": "OLEIC ACID:"}{"title": "JAMA INTERN MED:JAMA Intern Med is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to various aspects of internal medicine."}{"title": "CLIN THER:Clin Ther is a journal that publishes studies on clinical therapeutics, including treatments for cardiovascular conditions."}{"title": "PROC NATL ACA SCI USA:Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences USA publishes research across various scientific disciplines, including studies on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "CURRENT OPINION ENDOCRINOL DIAB OBES:Current Opinion in Endocrinology, Diabetes, and Obesity is a journal that reviews current research in these fields, including cardiovascular implications."}{"title": "CURRENT OPINION LIPIDOL:Current Opinion Lipidol, also known as Current Opinion in Lipidology, is a journal dedicated to providing reviews and opinions on lipid metabolism and related topics. It focuses on discussing research concerning lipids and their significant role in health, particularly in relation to cardiovascular disease. The journal serves as a platform for the latest insights and developments in the field of lipidology, contributing to the understanding of how lipids impact overall health."}{"title": "AHA SCIENTIFIC STATEMENT:The AHA Scientific Statement is a guideline published by the American Heart Association regarding fish consumption and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "VIRTANEN JK:Virtanen JK is an author of a study on mercury, fish oils, and cardiovascular disease in eastern Finland."}{"title": "WANG DD:Wang DD is an author of a study associating specific dietary fats with total and cause-specific mortality."}{"title": "CLARKE R:Clarke R is an author of a meta-analysis on dietary lipids and blood cholesterol."}{"title": "HOPKINS P:Hopkins P is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on the effects of dietary cholesterol on serum cholesterol."}{"title": "WEGGMANS RM:Weggmans RM is an author who studied the impact of dietary cholesterol from eggs on cholesterol ratios in humans."}{"title": "DJOUSSE L:Djouss\u00e9 L is an author who researched egg consumption in relation to cardiovascular disease and mortality."}{"title": "SHIN JY:Shin JY is an author of a systematic review and meta-analysis on egg consumption and diabetes risk."}{"title": "PLAT J:Plat J is an author discussing the therapeutic potential of plant sterols and stanols."}{"title": "LAW M:Law M is an author who evaluated the health effects of plant sterol and stanol margarines."}{"title": "GYLLING H:Gylling H is an author who studied retinol, vitamin D, carotene, and alpha-tocopherol in a hypercholesterolemic population."}{"title": "VAN HORN L:Van Horn L is an author of a scientific statement on dietary patterns to adhere to AHA/ACC guidelines."}{"title": "US DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES:The US Department of Health and Human Services provides dietary guidelines for Americans."}{"title": "APPEL LJ:Appel LJ is an author who studied the effects of protein, fat, and carbohydrate intake on blood pressure and serum lipids."}{"title": "SHRIDHAR K:Shridhar K is an author who researched the association between a vegetarian diet and cardiovascular disease risk factors in India."}{"title": "YOKOYAMA Y:Yokoyama Y is an author of a meta-analysis on vegetarian diets and blood pressure."}{"title": "JIAN ZH:Jian ZH is an author who studied the effects of a vegetarian diet on cholesterol and TAG levels by gender."}{"title": "ACUTE CORONARY EVENTS:Acute coronary events are critical health incidents that can be influenced by dietary intake, particularly fish oils and mercury."}{"title": "DIETARY GUIDELINES:Dietary guidelines provide recommendations for healthy eating patterns to improve health outcomes, including cardiovascular health."}{"title": "DIETARY CHOLESTEROL:Dietary cholesterol is a nutrient that has been evaluated for its impact on blood cholesterol levels and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "PLANT STEROLS:Plant sterols are compounds found in plants that may help lower cholesterol levels and improve heart health."}{"title": "FISH INTAKE:Fish intake is associated with various health outcomes, particularly in relation to cardiovascular disease risk."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VALL D'HEBRON:Hospital Universitario Vall d'Hebron is a prominent medical facility situated in Barcelona, Spain. It specializes in a range of medical fields, particularly pediatric gastroenterology, nutrition support, hepatology, and liver transplantation. Additionally, the hospital is involved in various medical treatments and research initiatives, focusing on nutritional support and metabolic disorders. This comprehensive approach underscores its commitment to advancing healthcare and providing specialized care to its patients."}{"title": "ROSA BURGOS PEL\u00c1EZ:Rosa Burgos Pel\u00e1ez is a medical professional associated with the Unidad de Soporte Nutricional at Hospital Universitario Vall d'Hebron."}{"title": "MIREIA GUERRERO GUAL:Mireia Guerrero Gual is a medical professional associated with the Unidad de Soporte Nutricional at Hospital Universitario Vall d'Hebron."}{"title": "GUILLERMO C\u00c1RDENAS LAGRANJA:Guillermo C\u00e1rdenas Lagranja is a medical professional associated with the Unidad de Soporte Nutricional at Hospital Universitario Vall d'Hebron."}{"title": "HEGOI SEGUROLA GURRUTXAGA:Hegoi Segurola Gurrutxaga is a medical professional associated with the Unidad de Soporte Nutricional at Hospital Universitario Vall d'Hebron."}{"title": "DIETAS CONTROLADAS EN \u00c1CIDOS GRASOS:Controlled diets in fatty acids are dietary interventions aimed at managing conditions like adrenoleucodistrofia by regulating the intake of specific fatty acids."}{"title": "PUBLIC HEALTH NUTR:Public Health Nutr is a peer-reviewed journal that focuses on research related to public health nutrition."}{"title": "X-ALD:X-ALD is a hereditary disorder linked to the X chromosome, characterized by an inability to degrade very long-chain fatty acids, leading to various clinical manifestations."}{"title": "ALDP:ALDP, or Adrenoleukodystrophy Protein, is a peroxisomal membrane protein that plays a crucial role in the transport of very long-chain fatty acids. Alterations in ALDP are associated with X-linked Adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD), a genetic disorder that affects the nervous system and adrenal glands. The study of ALDP is significant for both the diagnosis and understanding of X-ALD, highlighting its importance in the context of this disease."}{"title": "ADRENOMIELONEUROPAT\u00cdA:Adrenomieloneuropathy is a form of X-ALD that typically presents in young adults, characterized by progressive spastic paraparesis and sphincter disturbances."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE ADDISON:Addison's syndrome is a condition that can occur in about 10% of X-ALD patients, characterized by primary adrenal insufficiency without apparent neurological involvement."}{"title": "FORMA CEREBRAL INFANTIL:The childhood cerebral form of X-ALD is characterized by rapid progression of symptoms starting between ages 3 and 10, including hyperactivity and poor school performance."}{"title": "ADULT CEREBRAL:The adult cerebral form of X-ALD typically begins in the third decade of life and progresses similarly to the childhood form."}{"title": "ADRENOMIELONEUROPAT\u00cdA DEL ADULTO:Adult adrenomieloneuropathy usually presents in young adults with progressive spastic paraparesis and sphincter disturbances."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA ADRENOCORTICAL:Adrenal insufficiency is a common condition in X-ALD patients, often requiring study and treatment."}{"title": "CORTEX ADRENAL:The adrenal cortex is the outer part of the adrenal glands, which are responsible for producing hormones, and is affected in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "HEXA-COSANOIC ACID:Hexacosanoic acid (C26:0) is a very long-chain fatty acid that accumulates in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, contributing to the disease's pathology."}{"title": "TETRA-COSANOIC ACID:Tetracosanoic acid (C24:0) is another fatty acid that accumulates in lower amounts in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "AGCML:AGCML is a biochemical marker associated with adrenoleukodystrophy, a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. It is monitored during treatment to assess the condition of patients. AGCML refers specifically to very long-chain saturated fatty acids that accumulate in the bodies of individuals with adrenoleukodystrophy, leading to various health issues. These fatty acids can cause metabolic problems and are also linked to Reye-like syndrome, which further complicates the health of affected patients."}∞â0␀␀␀␀␀Xä0␀␀␀␀␀tä0␀␀␀␀␀ã0␀␀␀␀␀ãã0␀␀␀␀␀˚ã0␀␀␀␀␀Fé0␀␀␀␀␀—é0␀␀␀␀␀/è0␀␀␀␀␀ˆè0␀␀␀␀␀ë0␀␀␀␀␀úë0␀␀␀␀␀Ií0␀␀␀␀␀˘í0␀␀␀␀␀ƒî0␀␀␀␀␀kï0␀␀␀␀␀ñ0␀␀␀␀␀Äó0␀␀␀␀␀@ò0␀␀␀␀␀≥ò0␀␀␀␀␀Gô0␀␀␀␀␀ö0␀␀␀␀␀èö0␀␀␀␀␀õ0␀␀␀␀␀␀ù0␀␀␀␀␀ù0␀␀␀␀␀Ùù0␀␀␀␀␀™û0␀␀␀␀␀Xü0␀␀␀␀␀˚ü0␀␀␀␀␀¶†0␀␀␀␀␀:¢0␀␀␀␀␀£0␀␀␀␀␀ •0␀␀␀␀␀€•0␀␀␀␀␀•0␀␀␀␀␀¥ß0␀␀␀␀␀R®0␀␀␀␀␀˙®0␀␀␀␀␀H™0␀␀␀␀␀Û™0␀␀␀␀␀s´0␀␀␀␀␀Ê´0␀␀␀␀␀y¨0␀␀␀␀␀˜¨0␀␀␀␀␀q≠0␀␀␀␀␀Ê≠0␀␀␀␀␀vÆ0␀␀␀␀␀	Ø0␀␀␀␀␀óØ0␀␀␀␀␀ ∞0␀␀␀␀␀ù∞0␀␀␀␀␀±0␀␀␀␀␀r±0␀␀␀␀␀Œ±0␀␀␀␀␀C≤0␀␀␀␀␀ª≤0␀␀␀␀␀8≥0␀␀␀␀␀¢≥0␀␀␀␀␀=¥0␀␀␀␀␀ø¥0␀␀␀␀␀Jµ0␀␀␀␀␀´µ0␀␀␀␀␀∂0␀␀␀␀␀¢∂0␀␀␀␀␀-∑0␀␀␀␀␀∏∑0␀␀␀␀␀6∏0␀␀␀␀␀•∏0␀␀␀␀␀π0␀␀␀␀␀ïπ0␀␀␀␀␀∫0␀␀␀␀␀¢∫0␀␀␀␀␀%ª0␀␀␀␀␀œª0␀␀␀␀␀ôΩ0␀␀␀␀␀Cæ0␀␀␀␀␀Ÿæ0␀␀␀␀␀Äø0␀␀␀␀␀¿0␀␀␀␀␀°¿0␀␀␀␀␀˚¿0␀␀␀␀␀k¡0␀␀␀␀␀Ã¡0␀␀␀␀␀H¬0␀␀␀␀␀∑¬0␀␀␀␀␀8√0␀␀␀␀␀ç√0␀␀␀␀␀ƒ0␀␀␀␀␀nƒ0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁƒ0␀␀␀␀␀V≈0␀␀␀␀␀∞≈0␀␀␀␀␀.∆0␀␀␀␀␀Ø∆0␀␀␀␀␀«0␀␀␀␀␀t«0␀␀␀␀␀Â«0␀␀␀␀␀B»0␀␀␀␀␀ß»0␀␀␀␀␀…0␀␀␀␀␀s…0␀␀␀␀␀Â…0␀␀␀␀␀O 0␀␀␀␀␀π 0␀␀␀␀␀À0␀␀␀␀␀ÅÀ0␀␀␀␀␀¸À0␀␀␀␀␀GÕ0␀␀␀␀␀§Õ0␀␀␀␀␀ˇÕ0␀␀␀␀␀bŒ0␀␀␀␀␀∂Œ0␀␀␀␀␀≠–0␀␀␀␀␀—0␀␀␀␀␀’“0␀␀␀␀␀2”0␀␀␀␀␀Æ”0␀␀␀␀␀‘0␀␀␀␀␀R‘0␀␀␀␀␀ ‘0␀␀␀␀␀B’0␀␀␀␀␀¨’0␀␀␀␀␀÷0␀␀␀␀␀à÷0␀␀␀␀␀Á÷0␀␀␀␀␀◊0␀␀␀␀␀ö◊0␀␀␀␀␀dÿ0␀␀␀␀␀#Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀ú⁄0␀␀␀␀␀$€0␀␀␀␀␀›0␀␀␀␀␀ü›0␀␀␀␀␀@ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀[ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀Áﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀ãﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀‡0␀␀␀␀␀π‡0␀␀␀␀␀0·0␀␀␀␀␀©·0␀␀␀␀␀M‚0␀␀␀␀␀B‰0␀␀␀␀␀‡‰0␀␀␀␀␀ÀÂ0␀␀␀␀␀gÊ0␀␀␀␀␀Á0␀␀␀␀␀0Á0␀␀␀␀␀êË0␀␀␀␀␀•È0␀␀␀␀␀4Í0␀␀␀␀␀´Í0␀␀␀␀␀Î0␀␀␀␀␀ÜÎ0␀␀␀␀␀Ï0␀␀␀␀␀·Ì0␀␀␀␀␀üÓ0␀␀␀␀␀LÔ0␀␀␀␀␀◊Ô0␀␀␀␀␀e0␀␀␀␀␀Ò0␀␀␀␀␀§Ò0␀␀␀␀␀Û0␀␀␀␀␀üÛ0␀␀␀␀␀Ù0␀␀␀␀␀èÙ0␀␀␀␀␀Gı0␀␀␀␀␀ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀Øˆ0␀␀␀␀␀∫¯0␀␀␀␀␀Ö˘0␀␀␀␀␀:˙0␀␀␀␀␀›˙0␀␀␀␀␀~˚0␀␀␀␀␀¢˚0␀␀␀␀␀J¸0␀␀␀␀␀È¸0␀␀␀␀␀q˝0␀␀␀␀␀0˛0␀␀␀␀␀Ã˛0␀␀␀␀␀eˇ0␀␀␀␀␀ˆˇ0␀␀␀␀␀í␀1␀␀␀␀␀b1␀␀␀␀␀x1␀␀␀␀␀#1␀␀␀␀␀¡1␀␀␀␀␀Å1␀␀␀␀␀91␀␀␀␀␀„1␀␀␀␀␀j1␀␀␀␀␀r1␀␀␀␀␀∞1␀␀␀␀␀ﬂ	1␀␀␀␀␀I1␀␀␀␀␀Î1␀␀␀␀␀ç1␀␀␀␀␀>1␀␀␀␀␀˛1␀␀␀␀␀ñ1␀␀␀␀␀&1␀␀␀␀␀√1␀␀␀␀␀Â1␀␀␀␀